      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the altitude of the triangle, we can use the formula for the area of a triangle:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{altitude}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- The area of the triangle is 600 square feet.\n- The length of the base is 30 feet.\n\nWe need to find the altitude. Let's denote the altitude by \\( h \\). Substituting the given values into the area formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n600 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 \\times h\n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify the right-hand side of the equation:\n\n\\[\n600 = 15h\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( h \\), divide both sides of the equation by 15:\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{600}{15}\n\\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\n\\[\nh = 40\n\\]\n\nThus, the altitude of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{40}\\) feet.",
